{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22076-time-travel-and-you","id":22076,"title":"Time Travel and You","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-02T19:55:19-08:00","id":22076,"title":"Time Travel and You","content":"So there are a few things that I would like clarification on Time Travel in this setting. Specifically the Splinter timelines of Seattle (as it's pretty much the only part of the book that goes deep into the possibility).<br /> <br /> I figure other people have their own questions and hopefully I can give my oppinion as you all have helped me.<br /> <br /> so anyway:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>On Stigmatics: The book indicates that the timeline will make them not exist after 4 rotations of a repeated timeframe. Does this mean that they stop existing period or do they exist in the same way that travellers to this timeline from the main timeline do? ie they are completly out side of it.</li> <li>On Cryptids: how do cryptids work when they are created in a splinter?</li> <li>So the book indicates 2 ways that an Unchained can affect the main timeline through changes made in a splinter: By doing something physical and expending a dot of Willpower, and Pacts. Am I getting that right? or are there more? What if you never confront a, let's say a house wife, but you manipulate events (during that single year that that splinter encompass) to slowly erode at her sanity or the way she thinks on a given subject. After noticing a major change in her behavior, can the demon spend the dot to make that psychological harm affect the main timeline?</li> <li>When a Demon changes something in a splinter timeline, how does that stick if the demon decides to exit the splinter and enough time goes by that the shard starts the time over again? If I were to make an assumption, it would be that the events that were changed will come to pass through differrent events that don't neccessarily need the demon be present to inflict them. So if the demon destroys a building by blowing it up and spends the dot of will power and leaves to the present, some other, perhaps likeminded human (or otherwise) within the shard would set us up the bomb instead of the demon (this ofcoarse affects much more than just abuilding being blown up.</li> <li>Supernatural creatures within the shards. The book indicated that there are supernatural creatures in the shards same way as there are humans. So that would mean changelings and fae and mages. Do any of them have any sort of protection against the nature that they are in?</li> <li>On places: I wasn't quite sure. can a demon leave seattle in one of the shards? or does the map warp around somehow or do interesting flicks of space?</li> <li>On realms: so the book hinted that the shard had a shadow, access to the hedge, and it's own lower depths (if they were a part of that timeline). Does that mean that there is a separate Abyss and a separate Supernal? Perhaps just encompassing just the symbols that are represented in the shard?</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T02:54:46-08:00","id":22217,"title":"","content":"A couple of your questions are answered in the text.<br /> <br /> 1. Eventually they cease to be. Each repetition reorganizes reality such that they're less important, step by step, until they're taken out entirely.<br /> <br /> 6. The map warps around. It suggests the 1889 splinter has people coming in from outside, but the book is vague on where they come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T05:13:34-08:00","id":22271,"title":"","content":"If I may add a further question; what is the length of the 1889 shard? The original &quot;Sister Cities&quot; seed in the GMC implied it was a completely alternate timeline, but the Demon book has me confused. When does the 1889 splinter run from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T09:16:16-08:00","id":22376,"title":"","content":"@MythicFox but the wording is still unclear. do they lose their physical form and will never be seen again? or do they not exist according to that timeline like demons are when they visit. I'm getting confused with the wording. It says they cease to exist but they don't define what existing means in this context. According to that timeline shard, demon's don't exist but they still get to remain conscious and physical.<br /> <br /> EDIT: another question, if a demon needs to spend an extended amount of time in a splinter, does their cover erode when the cover isn't where it usually is supposed to be? (at work, at school, home for dinner ETC)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":".  Thought of more questions. 12-03-2013, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:51:07-08:00","id":22608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22076-time-travel-and-you?p=22376#post22376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It says they cease to exist but they don't define what existing means in this context.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ahhh, time travel. Always good for undermining the clarity of metaphysical terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T16:30:09-08:00","id":22704,"title":"","content":"In our changeling game, a dude was caught by a particularly nasty True Fae, and released after a torturous durance to a point before he was taken, so he can see it happen all over again, with his 'present' self being too arrogant to let anyone (including someone who purports to be himself) from changing the course of actions that leads to him being taken in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T03:50:51-08:00","id":23049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22076-time-travel-and-you?p=22271#post22271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may add a further question; what is the length of the 1889 shard? The original &quot;Sister Cities&quot; seed in the GMC implied it was a completely alternate timeline, but the Demon book has me confused. When does the 1889 splinter run from?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1889 splinter is a weird one. It's ongoing and doesn't reset and doesn't affect the dominant timeline in any way. The culture and technology don't advance at all, although it suggests that some aspects of the setting have 'evolved' from their original year (fashion norms, for instance). Also, the calendars all say 1930. I'm not official, but I personally take that to mean that calendar-wise, the year repeats but events don't. So even though December 31, 1930 was on a Wednesday and January 1, 1930 was also on a Wednesday, nobody notices that there are two Wednesdays in a row. (and perhaps time ran forward as normal -- real world standard normal -- until 1930, at which point certain things froze, but that's entirely personal speculation)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22076-time-travel-and-you?p=22376#post22376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MythicFox but the wording is still unclear. do they lose their physical form and will never be seen again? or do they not exist according to that timeline like demons are when they visit. I'm getting confused with the wording. It says they cease to exist but they don't define what existing means in this context. According to that timeline shard, demon's don't exist but they still get to remain conscious and physical.<br /> <br /> EDIT: another question, if a demon needs to spend an extended amount of time in a splinter, does their cover erode when the cover isn't where it usually is supposed to be? (at work, at school, home for dinner ETC)</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd take the book's lines of &quot;From the moment a stigmatic is created, a splinter reality starts writing him out of existence. A splinter stigmatic has only four reboots before he disappears entirely, with each successive reboot after the first removing him a degree further from all of his connections.&quot; and &quot;The fifth reboot erases him entirely.&quot; to mean exactly that. The stigmatic is no longer a part of that splinter. The splinter's history has been rewritten such that he has not only ceased to be but ceased to ever have been. He is gone forever. I would consider it a 'fixed change' that persists through the reboot, as per the text just above the sidebar about stigmatics and splinters.<br /> <br /> And as for your second question, I think it's one of those &quot;Depends on the Cover and depends on the Storyteller&quot; sorts of things. But given that a demon has to worry about Cover erosion for some of that stuff even without completely moving to an alternate reality, I'm pretty sure the answer is 'Yes.'<br /> <br /> Although I, in a game I was running, might hold off on compromise rolls for that sort of erosion until the demon returns. But that's solely because I like the dramatic impact and narrative possibilities of a demon losing track of time in a splinter and coming 'home' to find out they've made a Big Mistake.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, now that I have the PDF open, lemme take a moment to try and answer the rest of your original questions as best I can (but note that I'm not anyone official in this regard, just offering opinions based on what I'm looking at in the text):<br /> <br /> 2. Given that stigmatics and cryptids are very much alike, I'd probably suggest treating them the same.<br /> <br /> 3. Pacts and &quot;making a change in the physical realm and spending a dot of Willpower to make it stick&quot; seem to be the only ways. Indirect changes, like emotionall fallout from a change, is probably one of those 'time travel is wonky and a lot of stuff should be up to the Storyteller' sorts of things. (like whether or not stigmatics can escape)<br /> <br /> 4. Aside from the fact that I wouldn't consider blowing up a building to be a 'small-scale change,' your interpretation seems pretty straightforward.<br /> <br /> 5. There's nothing to suggest that other supernatural creatures are treated any differently than normal humans in a splinter. They likely have no clue that they're in an alternate timeline and aren't any more immune to the quirks of the splinter than anyone else (aside from stigmatics and demons).<br /> <br /> 7. Unless the Storyteller is playing with the cosmology, I'd argue that it's one 'set' of Supernal Realms and Abyss across all splinters just like with the Shadow, the Hedge, etc. (Especially since Imperial Mysteries says pretty firmly that the Hedge does connect to a portion of Supernal Arcadia)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T12:52:31-08:00","id":23272,"title":"","content":"Thank you! all of those answers are very very helpful for my chronicle. I just have one clarification question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22076-time-travel-and-you?p=23049#post23049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> to mean exactly that. The stigmatic is no longer a part of that splinter. The splinter's history has been rewritten such that he has not only ceased to be but ceased to ever have been. He is gone forever. I would consider it a 'fixed change' that persists through the reboot, as per the text just above the sidebar about stigmatics and splinters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So just to clarify when you say &quot;The stigmatic is no longer a part of that splinter.&quot; you mean that he stops having a physical form, stops being alive, and can no longer been seen or talked to or interacted with in any way.<br /> <br /> I only ask because in my mind, just because a splinter considers the stigmatic to not exist doesn't mean he stops existing in some fashion. I imagine that demons, when they go to a splinter, that splinter doesn't consider the demon to exist either and yet a demon can still walk around and interact.<br /> <br /> Although that might be an ST fiat type of thing. Sorry I get caught up on words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T13:26:03-08:00","id":23291,"title":"","content":"From my reading of it, it would seem that the stigmatic ceases to be. Completely and utterly unless he/she is taken out of the splinter before the final reset. I could be wrong but that's my interpretation. It seems that unlike say a demon who comes from outside the timeline (And is thus wholly apart from it) the stigmatic remains a part of the time line he resets but remembers the previous loop. this is a paradox if you will and the time line sets about removing the error marginalizing the errors impact on it's self with each reset until in can be rid of the error entirely. removing the stigmatic from the timeline and letting the final reset happen severs the connection. just my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1447-othikent","name":"Othikent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T14:10:28-08:00","id":23306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22076-time-travel-and-you?p=23272#post23272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! all of those answers are very very helpful for my chronicle. I just have one clarification question:<br /> <br /> <br /> So just to clarify when you say &quot;The stigmatic is no longer a part of that splinter.&quot; you mean that he stops having a physical form, stops being alive, and can no longer been seen or talked to or interacted with in any way.<br /> <br /> I only ask because in my mind, just because a splinter considers the stigmatic to not exist doesn't mean he stops existing in some fashion. I imagine that demons, when they go to a splinter, that splinter doesn't consider the demon to exist either and yet a demon can still walk around and interact.<br /> <br /> Although that might be an ST fiat type of thing. Sorry I get caught up on words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I mean there is no longer any physical form, no consciousness, they have been completely wiped from being. Aspects of the splinter universe may disregard a demon but demons can still exist in a splinter -- in the book, in fact, there are a couple of demons who live in splinters pretty much full-time. The God Machine, under the right circumstances, may still even notice the demon's presence if given a reason to. But when I say 'the stigmatic is no longer a part of that splinter,' I mean that they have no substance or being within that splinter any more. They have been eradicated. Utterly.<br /> <br /> Although that said, I can see an ST playing around with the physical laws of a splinter and force some poor bastard stigmatic to persist and maintain his memories in a looping timeline that disregards and doesn't remember him. (but then that means that the splinter stands a chance of accumulating stigmatics that can cause trouble unless they're somehow removed from the timeline)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T18:45:36-08:00","id":23439,"title":"","content":"I just had an incredible character idea pop into my head: a Demon whose Cover was that of a Soviet spy in the '62 splinter, who somehow stumbles out into the dominant timeline and must face a world where the Soviet Union has been fallen for twenty years. Potential Cipher: he takes &quot;what has Fallen may Rise again&quot; to refer to communism.<br /> <br /> I'm sure he and Comrade West would get along swimmingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T07:48:31-08:00","id":23753,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Thank you for the answers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T02:36:45-08:00","id":30346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22076-time-travel-and-you?p=23049#post23049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Given that stigmatics and cryptids are very much alike, I'd probably suggest treating them the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the Cryptid in the sample chronicle was trapped in the '62 splinter the entire time, I'd think they're different.<br /> <br /> Then again, it doesn't entirely differentiate between people who were already stigmatic before the splinter became a splinter and those who became stigmatic within the splinter. So, if someone became a stigmatic in 1959, when the '62 splinter was made, would they still see the God Machine, have their merits, etc. in every loop-though of the splinter's time-line? Or would they be slowly written out over the first four loop-throughs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}